body:
I am trying to get a modal window (ish) to close itself and it doesn't seem to do anything. I've tried using the `""` as the first part of the `.navigate()`, but no luck. And, I have `enableTracing` turned on, and it doesn't show any activity. It's like the `.navigate()` action isn't even doing anything. 

For reference:

```js
this.router.navigate(
    [
        "",
        {
            outlets: {
                inbox: null // <---- Doesn't seem to do anything (from WITHIN inbox).
            }
        }
    ],
    {
        relativeTo: this.activatedRoute
    }
);
```

I've opened a similar issue (https://github.com/angular/angular/issues/19547), didn't saw this one before ;p

I did some work around similar to the @tinchou but always going from root, it could be improved using promise instead of `setTimeout` for sure, but basically I do each step at time.

```js
justGo (...args) {
  this.router.navigate(['/']);
  args.map((arg, index) => {
    setTimeout(() => this.router.navigate(arg), 50 * (index + 1));
  });
}
```

And I use like that:

```html
<button (click)="this.routeService.justGo(['/promotions'], ['', { outlets: { modal: [...] } }])"></button>
```
